      How do millions of discrete, polymorphic DNA bases combine to produce continuous phenotypic variation, shape disease predisposition, and govern complex physiological systems? <strong>Statistical Genetics</strong> provides the foundational mathematical and probabilistic machinery that connects population-scale genotype matrices to quantitative traits, evolutionary fitness, and causal biological mechanisms.
    </p>

